<title>UK: Glynwed up as report notes director buying.</title>
<headline>Glynwed up as report notes director buying.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in engineering group Glynwed International Plc rose on Monday after a report in the Sunday Times highlighted recent purchases of shares in the company by directors including chief executive Bruce Ralph.</p>
<p>The stock was up 7p at 263, rebounding from a more than four-year low of 250p set on May 16. Volume reached 287,466 shares.  </p>
<p>The Sunday Times said investors may follow the lead of the Glynwed directors since the company, whose products include Aga cookers, should benefit from a recovery in the housing market.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
